+ * mdmon's shadow of the AMD bitmap: how it last wrote it, next to it on the
+ * same disk.  The AMD drivers do not always resync what mdmon left dirty:
+ * after Linux went down while writing, rcraid.sys 9.5.0.201 clears the
+ * bitmap at its start without checking the volume, and 9.3.3.218 checks
+ * the mirrors but not RAID5 parity (Windows in a VM, q4-judge95).  A shadow
+ * still dirty over a clean AMD bitmap tells so, and the volume is resynced
+ * as after a crash (amd_resync_start).  The sector is in the first page of
+ * the md bitmap area: the kernel writes only the bits after it, the AMD
+ * firmware and drivers nothing there (amd_mdbm).
